  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sumesh C Sukumaran vs Union Of India on 17 March, 2025 Author: C.S.Dias Bench: C.S.Dias Wp(C) No. 4433 Of 2025 1 2025:Ker:22640 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr.Justice C.S.Dias Monday, The 17Th Day Of March 2025 / 26Th Phalguna, 1946 Wp(C) No. 4433 Of 2025 Petitioner/S: Sumesh C Sukumaran Aged 37 Years S/O. Of Sukumaran, Charuvila Puthen Veedu, Ayyappancoil P.O., Ayyappancoil Village Idukki District, Pin - 685507 By Advs. George Mathew Praveen S. Sunil Kumar A.G Mathew K.T. George K.V. Boby Mathew Stephy K Regi Adithya Benzeer Medha B.S. John Zachariah Dominic Respondent/S: 1 Union Of India Rep. By Its Secretary To Government, Ministry Of Micro, Small And Medium Enterprises, Udyog Bhawan, Rafi Marg, New Delhi, Pin - 110011 Sumesh C Sukumaran vs Union Of India on 17 March, 2025 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/78589976/ 1 2 The Khadi And Village Industries Commission Kerala (State Office), Rep. By State Director, Tc No: 21/235, Vaydhuthi Bhavan, Pattom Palace P.O., Thiruvananthapuram, Pin - 695005 3 The Kerala Khadi And Village Industries Board Rep. By Its Nodal Officer (Pmegp), Vanchiyoor, Thiruvananathapuram, Pin - 695035 Wp(C) No. 4433 Of 2025 2 2025:Ker:22640 4 The District Industries Centre Idukki Rep. By Its General Manager, Mini Civil Station, Thodupuzha Taluk, Idukki District, Pin - 685584 5 South Indian Bank Kattapana Branch, Rep. By Its Branch Manager, Kp 1/640 A, Ward No.1 Kgees Building, Erattayar Road, Kattappana Po Idukki District, Kerala, Pin - 685508 By Adv T. Rajasekharan Nair",
    "facts": "The writ petition is filed to direct the respondents 2 to 5 to release the margin money (subsidy) kept in the petitioner's Term Deposit Receipt (TDR) account to the petitioner's loan account. 2. The petitioner had started a unit of Bee keeping, manufacturing and processing of honey unit under Ext.P1 Prime Minister's Employment Generation Programme ('PMEGP', in short). The Government subsidy under the Scheme is directed to be routed through the Khadi and Village Industries Commission - the 2 nd respondent. The petitioner was entitled to Rs.8,65,789/- as subsidy, which was paid to the petitioner's TDR account on 10.03.2020. The margin money has not been adjusted to the petitioner's loan account due to the delay in verification by the respondents. The 5 th WP(C) NO. 4433 OF 2025 2025:KER:22640 respondent has classified the petitioner's bank account as NPA. Yet, the subsidy kept in the TDR account is not adjusted to the petitioner's loan account. The 4 th respondent has ignored the petitioner's demand for the above course. The action on the part of the respondents is arbitrary. Hence, the writ petition.",
